<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lidice</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lidice is a village near Kladno in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, destroyed by the Nazis on 10 June 1942 in reprisal for the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reinhard-heydrich">Reinhard Heydrich</a>. The men were shot, the women sent to Ravensbrück <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camp</a> and most of the children murdered, and the village was razed. Its fate became a worldwide symbol of Nazi terror, and a new village was built nearby after the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lidice.jpg" alt="Lidice" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miaow Miaow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lidice_CZ_new_Lidice_municipal_office.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
